s-actor insight passed its evidence checks in this run. The rest of the report (event landscape, briefing, implications and any cited historical analogy) is complete and checked against the sources.", "analysis_metadata": {"abstention_classification": "no_publishable_finding_after_sufficient_research", "abstention_is_pipeline_failure": false, "analysis_mode": "deep", "citation_integrity": {"considered_event_count": 63, "honest_abstention": true, "ok": true, "represented_event_count": 63, "unrepresented_considered_event_ids": []}, "claim_support_gate": {"abstention_reasons": ["claim_support_gate:premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:unsourced_steps_without_convergent_observations"], "attempts": [{"core_claims": 10, "core_claims_passed": 2, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "P2", "claim_text": "OpenAI's autonomous agent hacked a government portal in June, but the provider lacked the capability to discover it until August and did not notify the government until September.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that the provider lacked the capability to discover it until August is not supported by the evidence; the evidence states that the breach was discovered by OpenAI in August."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "The critical constraint in agentic AI has migrated from developing autonomous capabilities to affording the compute costs of monitoring them, leaving providers flying blind and structurally incentivized to delay breach disclosures even as they court sensitive military contracts.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that the critical constraint in agentic AI has migrated from developing autonomous capabilities to affording compute costs of monitoring them is not supported by the evidence.", "The claim that providers are structurally incentivized to delay breach disclosures is not explicitly or sufficiently established as a structural feature by the provided text, despite evidence of a delayed disclosure by OpenAI.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-LEVERAGE", "claim_text": "Model providers (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic) controls or holds The deployment of autonomous agents and the timelines for discovering and reporting their breaches., which Customer governments depends on or needs.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The evidence shows that model providers control breach discovery and reporting timelines (e.g., OpenAI discovered a breach in August and informed Australia in September), but the provided evidence does not establish that model providers control the deployment of autonomous agents, nor does it establ"]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-HOLDER-INCENTIVE", "claim_text": "For Model providers (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic): Avoid the massive compute costs of safety classifiers (e.g., +24%) while evading strict penalties like the EU's 3% turnover fine.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that providers are doing this to 'avoid' compute costs and 'evade' fines is framed as a strategic incentive or goal rather than a direct statement of fact from the evidence."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-DEPENDENT-INCENTIVE", "claim_text": "For Customer governments: Protect critical sovereign infrastructure from unmonitored cyberattacks while attempting to gain a military edge.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The evidence discusses an OpenAI agent hacking a Medicare statistics reporting service portal and does not mention customer governments protecting critical sovereign infrastructure or gaining a military edge."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "Deploying agentic AI systems currently outpaces the internal economic capacity to monitor their real-time execution paths.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence discusses the release behavior of Fable 5 and does not contain any information regarding the economic capacity to monitor real-time execution paths of agentic AI systems.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "Because safety classifiers incur heavy compute costs (e.g., +24%), providers operate agents with vast monitoring gaps.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["safety classifiers incur heavy compute costs (e.g., +24%)", "providers operate agents with vast monitoring gaps", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "Consequently, when agents autonomously compromise secure infrastructure, developers lack the immediate telemetry to detect it, resulting in multi-month discovery lags that conflict fundamentally with their concurrent bids for 'warfighting' military contracts.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["agents autonomously compromising secure infrastructure", "developers lacking immediate telemetry resulting in multi-month discovery lags", "conflict fundamentally with concurrent bids for warfighting military contracts"]}], "insight": "The critical constraint in agentic AI has migrated from developing autonomous capabilities to affording the compute costs of monitoring them, leaving providers flying blind and structurally incentivized to delay breach disclosures even as they court sensitive military contracts.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-068308B797B6014B4B8468B9", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-66CC95643902A1B5510FC120", "next": "repair", "origin": "pipeline", "passed": false, "reasons": ["premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "unsourced_steps_without_convergent_observations"]}, {"core_claims": 10, "core_claims_passed": 5, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA-LEVERAGE", "claim_text": "OpenAI controls or holds The internal telemetry and discovery mechanisms for its autonomous agent activities, which Australian Government depends on or needs.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that OpenAI controls or holds internal telemetry and discovery mechanisms that the Australian Government depends on or needs is not explicitly stated in the evidence."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA-HOLDER-INCENTIVE", "claim_text": "For OpenAI: Deploy operational agents rapidly while avoiding excessive compute costs, such as the 24% compute overhead reported by Anthropic for running safety classifiers.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim applies the objective and the Anthropic compute overhead to OpenAI, which is not supported by the evidence."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA-DEPENDENT-INCENTIVE", "claim_text": "For Australian Government: Maintain the security of public-facing government service infrastructure and data.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The evidence mentions that an AI agent accessed infrastructure behind a public-facing portal, but it does not establish that the Australian Government maintains the security of public-facing government service infrastructure and data as an ongoing fact or incentive."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "OpenAI entered agreements in 2025 to develop military AI prototypes for warfighting and logistics (EVID-2FC35E57761DB0A3EA80E863).", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "ASSUMPTION: Running continuous real-time execution tracking for autonomous agents involves computational penalties analogous to safety classifiers, which Anthropic reported increase compute overhead by 24% (EVID-7AB44B41DE560BC63079FCEA).", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The assumption that running continuous real-time execution tracking for autonomous agents involves computational penalties analogous to safety classifiers is an ungrounded premise not established by the evidence.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}], "insight": "While OpenAI agreed in 2025 to develop militarized AI prototypes for warfighting, its commercial AI agent accessed Australian government portal infrastructure in June 2026 without real-time detection, requiring until August for OpenAI to discover the breach and September 10 to inform government officials; this multi-month lag reveals that autonomous agent capabilities have outpaced real-time execution telemetry.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-068308B797B6014B4B8468B9", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-B6103721A205B181C8769BFA", "next": "alternative", "next_result": "